  "id": "drive-theory",
  "term": "drive theory",
  "definition": "In this source, drive theory is a motivational framework, presented as an updated Freudian account, that explains addictive behavior as an effort to make up for an underlying biological deficit. It describes addiction as arising from a lack of a specific signaling molecule, with the behavior serving a compensatory drive.",
